00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:07.590
Are we going to have a shot of like some kind of alcohol and then jump in an icy lake?
我们要先喝一杯某种烈酒，然后跳进冰冻的湖里吗？

155
00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.630
I don't know if I'm at icy lake yet.
我不知道自己是不是已经能接受冰湖了。

156
00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:11.490
I mean, I'm at pretty cold.
我是说，我还算能接受挺冷的。

157
00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:12.590
Would you do it though?
不过你会去吗？

158
00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:13.030
No.
不会。

159
00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:14.250
Here's the thing.
情况是这样的。

160
00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:15.750
Lee is really into it.
李对这个非常热衷。

161
00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:20.010
Lee wants to talk to Josh about it because Josh, you know, is a super healthy guy.
李想跟乔什聊聊这个，因为你知道，乔什是个超级注重健康的人。

162
00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:20.350
Yeah.
是啊。

163
00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:23.170
I think he's going to get Josh to start doing it.
我觉得他会拉着乔什开始尝试呢。

164
00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:26.570
Lee and I think maybe 2022, we might get you to do it, Ange.
李和我猜也许2022年，我们可能会让你去试一试，安琪。

165
00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:27.130
No way.
绝不可能。

166
00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.110
I hate being cold.
我讨厌寒冷。

167
00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.250
I want it to be something that you do.
我希望那是你们做的事。

168
00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:30.930
No.
才不要。

169
00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.130
I don't know why.
我不知道为什么。

170
00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:34.590
I don't want to do it.
我可不想去。

171
00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:36.230
All right, fine.
好吧，行吧。

172
00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:39.010
I would do it on a vacation.
如果在度假的话我可能会去。

173
00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:40.790
I am vacation adventurous.
我在度假时很有冒险精神。

174
00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:42.390
I am not day-to-day adventurous.
我在日常生活中可没有什么冒险精神。

175
00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:43.090
All right.
好吧。

176
00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.550
Take me, you know, somewhere Nordic.
带我去那种具有北欧风情的地方吧。

177
00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:46.530
All right.
好吧。

178
00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:47.830
Maybe I'll jump in.
也许我会跳下去。

179
00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:48.530
All right.
好吧。

180
00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.810
And holler after I've had a shot of something.
而且在喝了一杯什么酒之后大喊大叫。

181
00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:54.570
Health routine you want.
你想要的健康养生。

182
00:07:56.030 --> 00:08:01.970
Well, today we are going to talk about The Meeting, which is season six, episode two.
好了，今天我们要聊的是《会议》，也就是第六季第二集。

183
00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:05.870
It is written by one of our favorite people, Aaron Schur.
本集由我们最喜欢的人之一亚伦·舒尔编剧。

184
00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:06.970
Love him.
超爱他。

185
00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.910
And directed by one of our other favorite people, Randall Einhorn.
并由我们另一位最喜欢的人兰多夫·艾恩霍恩执导。

186
00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:11.470
Yeah.
对的。

187
00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:12.830
Here's a summary.
以下是剧情梗概。

188
00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:16.750
Jim meets with David Wallace about a possible promotion.
吉姆与大卫·华莱士会面，商讨晋升的可能性。

189
00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:22.470
Dwight and Toby join forces to investigate whether Daryl submitted a fraudulent medical claim.
德怀特和托比联手调查达里尔是否提交了虚假医疗理赔。

190
00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:28.310
And Pam works to lock down her RSVPs for her and Jim's wedding.
而帕姆正忙着敲定她和吉姆婚礼的出席回执。

191
00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.530
I found that storyline so relatable.
我发现这条故事线简直太有共鸣了。

192
00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:32.870
Will you just RSVP, people?
大家就不能把回执交了吗？

193
00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:34.270
Just RSVP!
快交回执吧！

194
00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:37.170
When Meredith says, I'll just text you the day of the wedding.
当梅雷迪思说，我婚礼当天直接发短信给你。

195
00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:38.630
I know.
我知道。

196
00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:40.810
I mean, did you get texts on the day of your wedding?
我是说，你们在婚礼当天收到过短信吗？

197
00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:41.710
Because I did.
因为我收到过。

198
00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:46.610
I was like, you may not be my friend anymore, person who texted me on my wedding morning
当时我想，发短信问我停车指南什么的那个家伙，

199
00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:49.470
to ask me about, like, parking instructions.
你可能不再是我的朋友了。

200
00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:53.570
I got a text the morning of my wedding about, would this outfit be appropriate?
我在婚礼当天早上收到了一条短信，问这套衣服合适吗？

201
00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.370
What's the attire again?
请问着装要求是什么来着？

202
00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:56.610
Is it real fancy?
要穿得很正式吗？

203
00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:57.910
Or could I wear something casual?
还是我可以穿得休闲一点？

204
00:08:58.210 --> 00:08:59.090
See, now listen.
听我说，听好了。

205
00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:03.610
Ange, if you text me the morning of my wedding to ask me a question, that's fine.
安吉，如果你在我婚礼当天早上发信息来问我问题，那倒也行。

206
00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:04.350
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

207
00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:04.850
I wouldn't.
我才不会呢。

208
00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:07.130
That's the difference.
这就是区别所在。

209
00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:09.310
BFFs get a pass.
死党是有特权的。

210
00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.090
BFFs do get a pass, but they also know better.
死党确实有特权，但他们也应该懂得分寸。

211
00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:12.910
Yeah.
对啊。

212
00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:14.970
Text another wedding gueSt.
去发信息问别的婚礼宾客吧。

213
00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.410
You know someone who's going?
你知道有谁要去吗？

214
00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:16.810
Yeah.
知道。

215
00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:21.070
Text your most reliable friend who saved the invitation.
去问你那个最靠谱、还留着请柬的朋友。

216
00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:23.710
Text the friend you know in the wedding party.
去问你知道的那个身处婚礼伴郎伴娘团的朋友。

217
00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:24.230
Yeah.
对。

218
00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:24.750
Yeah.
是的。

219
00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:25.510
That's their job.
那是他们的工作。

220
00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:27.250
Leave the bride and groom alone.
别去打扰新郎新娘。

221
00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:27.810
Okay.
好吧。

222
00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.490
We could really go off on that.
我们真的可以就这个吐槽个没完。

223
00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:35.270
I mean, listen, clearly it meant so much to us, we moved it up to the top of the show.
我是说，听着，显然这对我们太重要了，我们把它提到了节目前面来讲。

224
00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:35.570
Yeah.
没错。

225
00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.190
We didn't even wait to get to that scene.
我们甚至都没等到播到那一幕。

226
00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:37.590
I know.
我知道。

227
00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:40.630
All right, let's do some fast facts.
好了，我们来播报几个快讯。

228
00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:47.590
Fast fact number one, this episode is going to kick off a major story arc for Jim, in which
快讯一，这一集将为吉姆开启一个重要的故事线，在此期间

229
00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:50.990
he becomes the co-manager of the Scranton branch.
他成为了斯克兰顿分公司的联合经理。

230
00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:54.950
Now, this is also going to signal a wardrobe change for Jim.
而这也标志着吉姆的着装将发生改变。

231
00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:55.710
Did you notice?
你注意到了吗？

232
00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:58.070
Boo-ba-doop-boo, wardrobe change.
嘟巴杜布嘟，换造型啦。

233
00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:02.970
Jim wears a jacket instead of his usual shirt and tie.
吉姆穿上了夹克，而不是他平时穿的衬衫和领带。

234
00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:04.730
Not just any jacket, a suit.
不仅仅是普通的夹克，是一套西装。

235
00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:05.490
Yeah.
对。

236
00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:08.610
This is going to continue while he is co-manager.
在他担任联合经理期间，这种情况会一直持续下去。

237
00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:11.390
I guess jacket means you take things seriously.
我猜穿夹克就代表你开始认真对待事情了。

238
00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:14.190
Look at Pam when she'd become a salesperson.
看看潘转行当销售的时候就知道了。

239
00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:15.550
They're the jacket couple now.
他们现在是夹克情侣了。

240
00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:16.270
We are.
我们是。

241
00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:17.750
We're so cute.
我们太可爱了。

242
00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:21.050
You know how Dwight wore his long sleeves for Charles Minor?
你知道德怀特为了查尔斯·迈纳穿长袖衬衫的事吗？

243
00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:21.710
Yeah.
知道。

244
00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:28.430
These are ways that our wardrobe department can really, you know, signal storytelling.
这些都是我们的服装部门真正能够用来传达剧情的方式。

245
00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:31.170
I think it's very cool, and I wanted to give them a shout out.
我觉得这非常酷，我想向他们致敬。

246
00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:31.950
Love it.
太棒了。

247
00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:33.090
Loved our wardrobe department.
我超爱我们的服装部门。

248
00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:34.510
I loved that fast fact.
我很喜欢这个快讯。

249
00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:35.930
Thank you, Ange.
谢谢你，安吉。

250
00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:42.170
Fast fact number two, this episode is a very interesting pairing as part of its B story.
快讯二，这一集作为其B故事，有一个非常有趣的组合。

251
00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:48.550
This feels like one of those assignments that we've heard about, the taking of the two people,
这感觉就像是我们听说过的那类任务，把两个人带走，

252
00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:50.230
Dwight and Toby.
德怀特和托比。

253
00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:53.950
When have we had a Dwight-Toby huge storyline?
我们什么时候有过德怀特和托比的主线剧情？

254
00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:55.110
I can't think of one.
我想不出来。

255
00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:55.220
I thought the same thing.
我也这么觉得。

256
00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:58.550
They were on a card, and they got sent off to the writer's pod.
他们在一张卡片上，然后被送到了编剧舱。

257
00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:04.650
Now, this B story was also ranked number seven on Screen Rant's Best B Plots.
现在，这个B支线在Screen Rant的最佳B支线排名中也位列第七。

258
00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:06.530
Do you know what was number one?
你知道第一名是什么吗？

259
00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:07.450
No.
不知道。

260
00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:09.170
Dwight's Concussion.
德怀特的脑震荡。

261
00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.010
Aw, with Pam.
噢，和帕姆一起。

262
00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:11.470
Yeah.
是的。

263
00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:12.810
I did love that one.
我确实很喜欢那一集。

264
00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:19.590
So, incidentally, while Paul Lieberstein was starring in this very popular B story,
所以，顺便说一句，当保罗·利伯斯坦在这个非常受欢迎的B支线中主演时，

265
00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:24.190
he was also our sole showrunner for this season, season six.
他也是我们这一季（第六季）的唯一剧集运作人。

266
00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:28.590
In season five, he shared that title with Jen Salata, but at this point,
在第五季，他与詹·萨拉塔共同担任此职，但到了这个时候，

267
00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:33.510
Jen was starting to develop some other projects, so she took a step back in season six.
詹开始开发其他一些项目，所以在第六季她退居二线了。

268
00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:35.310
She was the consulting producer.
她是顾问制片人。

269
00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:36.870
She worked three days a week.
她一周工作三天。

270
00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:41.670
So, Paul, our showrunner, was starring in this episode.
所以，保罗，我们的剧集运作人，在这一集中担任主演。

271
00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:42.570
I don't know.
我不知道。

272
00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:45.030
It just amazes me how he juggled it all.
我只是对他是如何兼顾这一切感到惊讶。

273
00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:47.430
I mean, I feel like he was living there for a bit.
我的意思是，我觉得他在那儿住了一段时间。

274
00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:49.310
Do you think he ever slept there?
你觉得他在那儿睡过觉吗？

275
00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:51.190
I feel like maybe at least once.
我觉得至少有一次吧。

276
00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:51.910
We should ask him.
我们应该问问他。

277
00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:52.630
We should ask.
我们应该问问。

278
00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:54.910
Now, fast fact number three.
现在，速记趣事第三条。

279
00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:56.590
Angela, I am handing over to you.
安吉拉，我把它交给你了。

280
00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:58.010
What would you like to tell us?
你想告诉我们什么？

281
00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:01.550
I would like to talk about the deleted scenes for this episode.
我想谈谈这一集的删减片段。

282
00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:05.510
I am titling this fast fact because I guess I titled my fast facts.
我给这个速记趣事起了个标题，因为我想我给我的速记趣事起过标题。

283
00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:06.050
Oh.
哦。

284
00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.790
I am titling my fast fact.
我正在为我的速记趣事起标题。

285
00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:09.590
Stay with me.
听我说完。

286
00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:11.550
Long, long, long, long.
长，长，长，长。

287
00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:12.850
Oh.
哦。

288
00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:15.170
Long, long, long, long, long.
长，长，长，长，长。

289
00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.090
Should I be titling my fast facts?
我是不是该给我的速记趣事起标题？

290
00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:19.090
No.
不。

291
00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:21.690
I think we're all fine not to.
我觉得我们不这样做都挺好的。

292
00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:26.010
You guys, this episode was a very long script.
伙计们，这一集的剧本非常长。

293
00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:26.690
Oh.
哦。

294
00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:31.490
And a lot of our scripts came in very long, but I just thought this one really highlights
我们的很多剧本交上来的时候都很长，但我只是觉得这一集真正突显了

295
00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:36.030
how much didn't make it in that was written on the page, and I wanted to share that with you.
写在纸上却有很多没有被采用的内容，我想和大家分享这一点。

296
00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:36.610
Okay.
好的。

297
00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:41.070
It's a little insight, you guys, into the deleted scenes of an episode of The Office.
伙计们，这是一个关于《办公室》单集删减片段的小小见解。

298
00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:46.110
So I was trading emails with Randy Cordray, and he said that there was so much material
所以我跟兰迪·科德雷发邮件交流，他说我们的剧集有太多的素材，

299
00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:52.290
for our episodes that our editor's first cuts were usually about 45 minutes long.
以至于我们剪辑师的初剪通常都有大约45分钟长。

300
00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:57.390
And we had to narrow that down to 21 minutes and 30 seconds to broadcast the show.
我们必须将其缩减到21分30秒才能播出。

301
00:12:57.510 --> 00:13:00.110
So they would cut more than half.
所以他们会砍掉一半以上。

302
00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:00.970
Exactly.
没错。

303
00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:02.730
That brings me to this script.
这就说到了我手里的这份剧本。

304
00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:03.630
Jenna, I looked.
珍娜，我看了。

305
00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:05.710
The shooting draft was 41 pages.
拍摄剧本有41页。

306
00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:08.850
Okay, so it's usually a page equals a minute.
好吧，通常一页就是一分钟。

307
00:13:09.090 --> 00:13:10.310
We've talked about that before.
我们以前讨论过这个。

308
00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:10.790
Right.
对。

309
00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:13.790
So they were going to have to edit out more than half the script.
所以他们不得不把剧本砍掉一半以上。

310
00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:19.470
I went to the shooting draft, and I read the shooting draft as I watched the episode that
我看了拍摄剧本，我一边读着拍摄剧本，一边看着播出的

311
00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:26.670
was broadcast, and there were six talking heads that never made it in, eight full scenes
那一集，里面有六个单人采访镜头被删了，八个完整的场景

312
00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:32.730
that never made it, and then five scenes were actually extended and longer than what made
被删了，还有五个场景实际上比最终播出的

313
00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:33.530
it onto the screen.
版本要长。

314
00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:39.070
And I was trading emails with Randy, and he brought up a great, great note, which is the
我当时在和兰迪发邮件，他提出了一个非常非常棒的意见，那就是

315
