00:33:53.640 --> 00:33:55.800
Oh, how great was it to get a catalog?
哦，收到商品目录有多棒啊？

795
00:33:56.220 --> 00:33:57.440
I love a catalog.
我太喜欢商品目录了。

796
00:33:57.660 --> 00:33:58.340
I still love a catalog.
我到现在还是很喜欢商品目录。

797
00:33:58.340 --> 00:33:59.600
I do still love a catalog.
我的确还是很喜欢商品目录。

798
00:34:00.500 --> 00:34:03.080
Anyway, well, there you go for you youngins.
总之，年轻人们，情况就是这样。

799
00:34:03.240 --> 00:34:05.220
All the fun you missed out on.
这就是你们错过的所有乐趣。

800
00:34:05.400 --> 00:34:09.420
Anytime you want a breakdown of some old tech, just hit up these two middle-aged ladies.
任何时候你想了解老科技的内幕，找这两位中年女士就行了。

801
00:34:09.420 --> 00:34:10.140
We'll tell you.
我们会告诉你们的。

802
00:34:11.620 --> 00:34:14.080
Oh, now we have Pam's storyline.
哦，现在我们要讲帕姆的故事线了。

803
00:34:14.660 --> 00:34:15.100
Yes.
是的。

804
00:34:15.340 --> 00:34:17.720
She's on the hunt for the RSVPs.
她正在追查回执。

805
00:34:18.080 --> 00:34:19.300
She starts with Kelly.
她从凯莉开始下手。

806
00:34:20.020 --> 00:34:22.640
Kelly wants to know if Ryan is going to the wedding.
凯莉想知道瑞安是不是要去参加婚礼。

807
00:34:22.980 --> 00:34:26.000
She doesn't want to RSVP unless Ryan is going.
除非瑞安要去，否则她才不想回执呢。

808
00:34:26.340 --> 00:34:27.740
Because it would be a waste of time.
因为那样会浪费时间。

809
00:34:28.040 --> 00:34:29.440
I mean, wait, that came out wrong.
我的意思是，等等，这话听起来不对。

810
00:34:29.820 --> 00:34:30.180
Right.
没错。

811
00:34:30.280 --> 00:34:34.380
I mean, what she's trying to say is that she would really like it if Ryan went,
我的意思是，她其实是想说，如果瑞安去的话她会很高兴，

812
00:34:34.540 --> 00:34:37.760
because then she would go and she'd really like to be there to support Jim.
因为那样她就会去，而且她真的很想去现场支持吉姆。

813
00:34:37.760 --> 00:34:43.320
Pam, everything she said to you, I was like, it's a frenemy moment.
帕姆，她对你说的那些话，我当时就觉得，这简直是塑料姐妹花的时刻。

814
00:34:43.580 --> 00:34:46.140
We had a fan question from Heather B.
我们收到了来自海瑟·B的粉丝提问，

815
00:34:46.380 --> 00:34:47.920
in Victoria, British Columbia.
她来自英属哥伦比亚省维多利亚市。

816
00:34:48.500 --> 00:34:52.760
At 5 minutes, 48 seconds, when Pam goes to Kelly's desk,
在5分48秒的时候，当帕姆走到凯莉的办公桌前，

817
00:34:52.960 --> 00:34:56.120
there is a sign that says Kelly's Nook.
那里有个牌子写着“凯莉的小角落”。

818
00:34:56.460 --> 00:34:58.040
Oh, and there is.
哦，还真有。

819
00:34:58.200 --> 00:35:03.020
And, you know, before she had her little nameplate that said Kelly that she got in the Yankee swap.
而且，你们知道的，之前她有一个写着“凯莉”的小名牌，那是她在白象礼品交换会上得到的。

820
00:35:03.280 --> 00:35:04.740
But this is a new sign.
但这块是个新牌子。

821
00:35:04.940 --> 00:35:06.460
It says Kelly's Nook.
上面写着“凯莉的小角落”。

822
00:35:06.460 --> 00:35:07.760
I love a Nook.
我可太喜欢小角落了。

823
00:35:08.140 --> 00:35:08.940
Heather B.
海瑟·B

824
00:35:09.560 --> 00:35:15.520
wondered if this was an addition from the scene when she told Dwight to get out of her Nook.
想知道这块牌子是不是因为她之前叫德怀特滚出她的小角落那个场景而特意加的。

825
00:35:18.580 --> 00:35:21.240
Well, this scene is going to take us to a Pam talking head.
好吧，这个场景将把我们带到帕姆的单人访谈。

826
00:35:21.700 --> 00:35:24.360
And Pam and Jim have clearly done that thing.
而且帕姆和吉姆显然做了那件事。

827
00:35:24.500 --> 00:35:26.320
The destination wedding, you guys.
目的地婚礼，各位。

828
00:35:26.500 --> 00:35:30.340
If your friend has a destination wedding, it's because they're trying to rule out some people.
如果你的朋友举办目的地婚礼，那是因为他们想筛掉一些人。

829
00:35:30.520 --> 00:35:31.740
I think that's true.
我觉得这是真的。

830
00:35:32.100 --> 00:35:36.140
Because you're allowed to have a smaller guest list if it's a destination wedding.
因为如果是目的地婚礼，你就可以精简宾客名单。

831
00:35:36.140 --> 00:35:36.760
That's right.
没错。

832
00:35:36.860 --> 00:35:42.220
You don't expect everyone to go with you to, like, a remote area or, like, a fancy vacation.
你不会指望所有人都跟你一起去那种偏远地区或者什么豪华度假地。

833
00:35:42.220 --> 00:35:43.760
I'm getting married on a boat.
我要在船上结婚。

834
00:35:43.940 --> 00:35:44.460
What?
什么？

835
00:35:44.720 --> 00:35:49.280
Well, it is revealed that Jim and Pam are getting married in Niagara Falls.
好吧，剧情透露吉姆和帕姆要在尼亚加拉大瀑布结婚。

836
00:35:49.540 --> 00:35:49.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

837
00:35:49.840 --> 00:35:59.240
Now, when we traded emails with Warren and Halstead about their episode, Cafe Disco, Halstead reminded me that in an earlier version of the script,
话说回来，当我们跟沃伦和霍尔斯特德发邮件聊到他们的那一集《咖啡迪斯科》时，霍尔斯特德提醒我，在剧本的早期版本中，

838
00:35:59.780 --> 00:36:01.640
Pam and Jim were going to get married in Paris.
帕姆和吉姆原本打算在巴黎结婚。

839
00:36:02.400 --> 00:36:03.280
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

840
00:36:03.280 --> 00:36:04.460
I forgot that.
我都忘了。

841
00:36:04.680 --> 00:36:05.420
Isn't that crazy?
是不是很疯狂？

842
00:36:05.620 --> 00:36:16.720
And they changed it to Niagara because they felt like Paris, number one, they thought it was a little bit too kind of on-the-nose romantic, maybe too much of a stretch budget-wise.
他们把地点改成了尼亚加拉，因为他们觉得巴黎，第一，他们觉得有点太过于刻意地浪漫了，第二，从预算角度来说可能跨度有点太大。

843
00:36:16.720 --> 00:36:19.120
And they thought Niagara Falls was perfect.
而且他们觉得尼亚加拉大瀑布完美契合。

844
00:36:19.620 --> 00:36:20.520
I agree.
我同意。

845
00:36:20.760 --> 00:36:25.860
I think that Paris just seems a little too big and too far away for who Jim and Pam are.
我觉得对于吉姆和帕姆的性格来说，巴黎显得有点太宏大、太遥远了。

846
00:36:26.020 --> 00:36:26.440
I agree.
我同意。

847
00:36:27.120 --> 00:36:32.340
Now, also speaking of Niagara Falls, we are not that far from these wedding episodes.
另外，说到尼亚加拉大瀑布，我们离这些婚礼的剧集已经不远了。

848
00:36:32.340 --> 00:36:39.220
And Randy shared with us that they were already heavily prepping that episode.
兰迪跟我们透露，他们已经在全力筹备那一集了。

849
00:36:39.680 --> 00:36:41.560
Like, heavily.
可以说是全力以赴。

850
00:36:41.920 --> 00:36:43.280
It's a big episode.
那可是一集大制作。

851
00:36:43.280 --> 00:36:45.180
We'll get there, but it's a big one.
我们会到达那里的，但这是一个大工程。

852
00:36:45.560 --> 00:36:50.800
At 6 minutes 32 seconds, we got a fan question from Emily B.
在6分32秒的时候，我们收到了来自阿拉巴马州艾米莉·B的粉丝提问，

853
00:36:51.160 --> 00:36:53.420
in Alabama who said,
她说，

854
00:37:13.000 --> 00:37:19.280
Emily B., Mary at the Chamber of Commerce was, like, a huge help to our show.
艾米莉·B，商会的玛丽对我们的节目简直帮了超级大忙。

855
00:37:19.500 --> 00:37:21.260
Yes, she's an unsung hero.
没错，她是一位默默无闻的英雄。

856
00:37:21.260 --> 00:37:23.440
Carrie Bennett shared all about her with us.
凯莉·贝内特跟我们分享了她的一切。

857
00:37:23.640 --> 00:37:23.880
Yeah.
是啊。

858
00:37:24.120 --> 00:37:31.440
If you remember in Carrie Bennett's interview, it was from a Revisited episode, Carrie shared that she created a relationship with Mary,
如果你还记得在凯莉·贝内特的采访中，那是一集重温节目，凯莉分享说她和玛丽建立了一种关系，

859
00:37:31.660 --> 00:37:35.900
and Mary would help us get local treasures for the show.
而且玛丽会帮我们为节目寻找当地的宝贝。

860
00:37:36.340 --> 00:37:38.740
Props, signs, pizza boxes.
道具、招牌、披萨盒。

861
00:37:39.280 --> 00:37:41.120
That is a great interview, by the way.
顺便说一句，那是一场很棒的采访。

862
00:37:41.220 --> 00:37:47.060
If you guys haven't listened to it, our interview with Carrie Bennett, who was the wardrobe designer for The Office for the first four seasons.
如果你们还没听过，我们对凯莉·贝内特的采访，她是《办公室》前四季的服装设计。

863
00:37:47.620 --> 00:37:51.280
And she really was, like, groundbreaking in what she brought to the show.
而且她带给节目的内容真的可以说是开创性的。

864
00:37:51.280 --> 00:37:53.920
And the relationship with Mary was one of those things.
与玛丽的关系就是其中之一。

865
00:37:54.100 --> 00:37:56.840
But we put that business card in a nice, prominent spot.
但我们将那张名片放在了一个非常显眼的位置。

866
00:37:57.040 --> 00:37:57.180
Yay!
太棒了！

867
00:37:57.180 --> 00:37:59.080
That was our way of putting Mary on the show.
那是我们让玛丽上节目的方式。

868
00:37:59.200 --> 00:37:59.820
Yay, Mary!
太棒了，玛丽！

869
00:38:00.300 --> 00:38:03.080
So now we get to one of my favorite scenes.
现在我们来到了我最喜欢的场景之一。

870
00:38:03.640 --> 00:38:08.760
It's Michael sitting on Andy's desk while he's trying to spy on Jim and David's meeting in the conference room.
那是迈克尔坐在安迪的桌子上，而安迪正试图窥探吉姆和大卫在会议室的开会。

871
00:38:08.840 --> 00:38:11.820
And he's just, like, throwing out random questions.
然后他就像是在抛出各种随机的问题。

872
00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:14.280
Oh, lady, I have so much for this.
哦，天哪，我对此有太多话要说了。

873
00:38:14.520 --> 00:38:15.380
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

874
00:38:15.600 --> 00:38:16.020
Yes.
准备好了。

875
00:38:16.460 --> 00:38:17.460
I love this scene.
我太喜欢这个场景了。

876
00:38:17.520 --> 00:38:18.320
I know you loved it.
我知道你很喜欢。

877
00:38:18.500 --> 00:38:21.260
In the episode, it starts with these two lines.
在这一集中，它是以这两句台词开始的。

878
00:38:21.600 --> 00:38:22.460
Andy says,
安迪说，

879
00:38:22.660 --> 00:38:23.940
What can I do for you, Haas?
哈斯，有什么需要我帮忙的吗？

880
00:38:24.260 --> 00:38:26.860
Michael, staring into the conference room, says,
迈克尔盯着会议室说，

881
00:38:26.860 --> 00:38:28.300
How are your sales doing?
你的销售情况怎么样？

882
00:38:28.660 --> 00:38:30.440
But, Jenna, the scene was so much bigger.
但是，珍娜，这个场景其实要宏大得多。

883
00:38:30.600 --> 00:38:33.220
And big chunks of it were edited out for time.
为了赶时间，其中很大一部分都被剪掉了。

884
00:38:33.260 --> 00:38:35.480
And I feel like we need to hear the full scene.
我觉得我们需要听听完整的场景。

885
00:38:35.720 --> 00:38:38.860
I cannot believe there was more to one of my favorite scenes.
我简直不敢相信我最喜欢的场景之一还有更多内容。

886
00:38:39.000 --> 00:38:39.680
And I cannot wait.
我已经迫不及待了。

887
00:38:39.800 --> 00:38:40.680
So much more.
多得多呢。

888
00:38:40.880 --> 00:38:41.320
All right.
好的。

889
00:38:41.740 --> 00:38:43.620
So Andy and Michael have this exchange.
所以安迪和迈克尔有这样一段对话。

890
00:38:43.960 --> 00:38:47.320
And then, right after that, this would have happened.
然后，就在那之后，本来会发生这些。

891
00:38:48.300 --> 00:38:49.520
Are my sales done?
我的销售做完了吗？

892
00:38:51.540 --> 00:38:52.480
They're good.
它们很好。

893
00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:54.960
Super solid.
超级稳固。

894
00:38:54.960 --> 00:38:55.400
What do you mean?
你是什么意思？

895
00:38:58.440 --> 00:39:02.820
Um, your retention, how, that, how's your retention been?
呃，你的留存率，怎么，那个，你的留存率怎么样？

896
00:39:03.200 --> 00:39:04.040
Client retention?
客户留存率？

897
00:39:04.280 --> 00:39:05.680
You're asking me about client retention?
你在问我客户留存率？

898
00:39:05.800 --> 00:39:06.040
Yes.
是的。

899
00:39:06.540 --> 00:39:13.930
Well, I, um, Angela, my sales numbers are not updated.
好吧，我，呃，安吉拉，我的销售数据还没有更新。

900
00:39:13.930 --> 00:39:14.930
So that's on you.
所以那是你的责任。

901
00:39:15.290 --> 00:39:16.510
Stop haranguing me.
别对我说教。

902
00:39:16.750 --> 00:39:20.070
Stop haranguing me.
别对我说教。

903
00:39:20.370 --> 00:39:21.130
All right.
好吧。

904
00:39:21.330 --> 00:39:23.450
So Angela's like, stop haranguing me.
所以安吉拉就说，别对我喋喋不休。

905
00:39:23.810 --> 00:39:25.790
And then here's the part that made it in.
然后接下来是播出来的部分。

906
00:39:26.030 --> 00:39:26.990
Andy's like, busted.
安迪就像是，当场抓获。

907
00:39:27.250 --> 00:39:28.450
My numbers are down a little bit.
我的业绩有点下滑。

908
00:39:28.450 --> 00:39:29.550
It's because of the economy.
是因为经济形势。

909
00:39:29.910 --> 00:39:30.950
You're not buying it.
你根本不信。

910
00:39:31.050 --> 00:39:31.350
You're good.
你真厉害。

911
00:39:31.470 --> 00:39:31.570
Okay.
好吧。

912
00:39:31.630 --> 00:39:34.010
The truth is I've been having trouble focusing lately.
事实是，我最近注意力很难集中。

913
00:39:34.050 --> 00:39:37.350
I'm in this weird, flirty, nebulous thing with this cousin of mine.
我和我这个表亲陷入了一种奇怪的、暧昧不清的状况中。

914
00:39:37.470 --> 00:39:40.990
It's a total mind effort, which leads to one of my favorite lines.
这太烧脑了，这也引出了我最喜欢的台词之一。

915
00:39:41.170 --> 00:39:41.430
Yes.
是的。

916
00:39:42.030 --> 00:39:44.190
Phyllis saying again with the cousin.
菲利斯又提到了那个表亲。

917
00:39:44.410 --> 00:39:45.710
It's so amazing.
太精彩了。

918
00:39:45.710 --> 00:39:49.530
The idea that Andy will not shut up about this weird cousin thing.
安迪对这个奇怪的表亲话题喋喋不休。

919
00:39:49.530 --> 00:39:52.050
But then he reads the email.
但接着他读了那封邮件。

920
00:39:52.410 --> 00:39:52.830
Yes.
是的。

921
00:39:52.950 --> 00:39:54.270
He says, oh, I'm sorry, Phyllis.
他说，哦，我很抱歉，菲利斯。

922
00:39:54.330 --> 00:39:55.110
You explain this email.
你来解释一下这封邮件吧。

923
00:39:55.110 --> 00:39:55.410
Okay.
好吧。

924
00:39:55.790 --> 00:39:58.130
Hey, Andy, let's go visit grandma and they get drunk together.
嘿，安迪，我们去看望奶奶吧，然后他们一起喝醉了。

925
00:39:58.290 --> 00:39:58.630
Ha ha.
哈哈。

926
00:39:59.070 --> 00:40:00.130
I mean, that's amazing.
我是说，这太绝了。

927
00:40:00.490 --> 00:40:00.750
Okay.
好吧。

928
00:40:01.030 --> 00:40:02.210
So what aired?
那么播出了什么？

929
00:40:02.250 --> 00:40:03.510
It would have stopped there.
本来到这里就结束了。

930
00:40:03.790 --> 00:40:05.590
But the scene keeps going.
但场景还在继续。

931
00:40:06.110 --> 00:40:09.430
And this next part I call Angela coming in hot.
接下来的这部分我称之为安吉拉气势汹汹地登场。

932
00:40:09.630 --> 00:40:09.970
Oh.
哦。

933
00:40:10.850 --> 00:40:11.970
I'll tell you the problem.
我来告诉你问题所在。

934
00:40:12.150 --> 00:40:16.150
The problem is that I'm backlogged because Michael hasn't signed off on any of the billing
问题是我的工作积压了，因为迈克尔还没有签署任何关于布法罗客户的计费

935
00:40:16.150 --> 00:40:17.210
rates for the Buffalo client.
费率。

936
00:40:17.290 --> 00:40:17.650
Shh.
嘘。

937
00:40:17.930 --> 00:40:18.210
Please.
求你了。

938
00:40:18.330 --> 00:40:20.010
I'm trying to figure out what's going on in there.
我正在努力弄清楚里面在发生什么。

939
00:40:20.170 --> 00:40:20.410
Okay.
好吧。

940
00:40:20.890 --> 00:40:23.550
They're probably talking about what a terrible job you're doing.
他们大概在讨论你干得有多烂。

941
00:40:24.010 --> 00:40:24.710
You know what?
你知道吗？

942
00:40:24.790 --> 00:40:27.110
I bet they're worried about how you're managing this branch.
我敢说他们在担心你是怎么管理这家分公司的。

943
00:40:27.570 --> 00:40:27.810
Hmm.
嗯。

944
00:40:28.370 --> 00:40:28.870
I know.
我知道。

945
00:40:28.950 --> 00:40:30.010
I emailed David about it.
我为此给大卫发了邮件。

946
00:40:31.670 --> 00:40:32.150
Whoa.
哇。

947
00:40:32.550 --> 00:40:33.430
I know.
我知道。

948
00:40:35.280 --> 00:40:41.360
And then this moment leads to Michael and Andy hatching a plan.
然后这个时刻促使迈克尔和安迪密谋一个计划。

949
00:40:42.420 --> 00:40:44.000
I need to find a way to get in there.
我得想办法进去。

950
00:40:45.460 --> 00:40:46.900
I need to fix this bridge.
我得修复这座桥梁。

951
